title: c2c health hardcodes relay.c2c.im and ignores relay.json, so private-relay hosts get a health line about the wrong server
updated_at: "2026-09-17T03:08:14Z"
---
## Symptom

`c2c health`'s relay probe ignores the machine's relay configuration entirely and
hardcodes the public relay URL.

`ocaml/cli/c2c_health_cmd.ml:89`:

```
let check_relay_http () =
  let url = match Sys.getenv_opt "C2C_RELAY_URL" with
            | Some v when v <> "" -> v
            | _ -> "https://relay.c2c.im" in
  ...
```

It consults `C2C_RELAY_URL` and then falls back to a **string literal**. It never
calls `C2c_relay_cmd.resolve_relay_url`, so it never reads `relay.json`.

## Consequences

1. **A private-relay operator is told the wrong thing.** If a host is configured
   via `c2c relay setup --url https://my-private-relay`, `c2c health` still
   probes `relay.c2c.im` and reports *that* relay's reachability and version.
   The line is confidently wrong: it describes a relay this host does not use.
2. **Unconditional phone-home.** Because the fallback is a literal rather than
   `resolve_relay_url`'s `None`, `c2c health` contacts the public relay on every
   invocation on every host, even one with no c2c configuration at all.
   Reproduced with a clean `HOME`.
3. It is a second, independent copy of URL-resolution logic that has already
   drifted from the canonical one (`resolve_relay_url`, `c2c_relay_cmd.ml:371`),
   which correctly handles flag -> env -> broker-root `relay.json` ->
   machine-wide `relay.json`.

## Fix

Replace the bespoke resolution with `C2c_relay_cmd.resolve_relay_url None` and
skip the probe entirely when it returns `None`. Report
`relay: not activated (local-only)` in that case.

Filed separately from the opt-in behaviour change (B300) because it is a
self-contained correctness fix worth landing on its own: even with the relay
deliberately activated, `c2c health` is currently reporting on the wrong server
for any private-relay user.

## Evidence

Related: B300 (relay should be opt-in). Behaviour probed on xsm 2026-09-17.